TEST 38093 -- MRP ring with DUT as MRM
===========================================================================
Run: 2026-09-30 14:32-14:59 NZDT, tb470, hand-driven (no framework script), queue row 9.
Tester: bench-runner. Case text: AWPTCM-T38093 (ck.db zephyr_cases), 9 steps.
Device clocks are UTC and run ~42 s ahead of tb470 (SA port-down 01:40:00 vs
tb470 shut stamp 14:39:18 NZDT = 01:39:18 UTC).

VERDICT: FAIL -- labelled CLEAN (reproduced 3 times; two method substitutions,
below, that do not touch what failed).

  The DUT as MRM does the job the steps ask for: the ring is operational after the
  save, a forwarding-port shutdown recovers in 70-108 ms, the ring re-blocks one port
  when the link returns, and after save + reboot the ring comes back and traffic is
  received. BUT every time the ring CLOSES -- a restored link (steps 8, repeat) or
  the post-boot ring-up (step 9) -- the MRM's own log shows
      Ring closed -> FSM CHK_RC -> CHK_RO evt=MRP_ProtEvTestTimerExpired -> Ring opened
  and it sets the returning port Forwarding while the other ring port is Forwarding
  too. VLAN 1 then LOOPS for 42-303 ms: one broadcast frame arrived up to 410 times,
  and each host NIC received its own frames back. After the reboot the DUT logged
  `Thrash-limiting: Disabled learning on sa2 ... port1.0.2 ... port1.0.9 on vlan 1`,
  its own loop evidence. A further false "Ring opened" fired 39 s after the ring had
  closed, with no event on the bench at all.
  FAIL CONDITION: MRP exists to keep the ring loop-free; here the MRM itself creates
  the loop, on every ring closure. That is the same false test-timer expiry as
  T28863 (28863.log), seen here without any stack membership change. The
  loop test is the one row 15 used: the same frame arriving more than once, and
  frames returning to the NIC that sent them. Neither happens in the baseline or in
  steady state. No threshold was invented.
  Terrence may re-grade: on the literal "expected" columns alone (the 200 ms
  profile is the only recovery bound available) every step would PASS.

