READING
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  - Failover (a link going DOWN) is fast and clean: 70-108 ms, no duplicates.
  - Every ring CLOSURE loops. At link-up the MRM goes to CHK_RC, its test timer
    expires before its own test frames return, it declares "Ring opened" and forwards
    BOTH ring ports; the MRC has already set its port Forwarding, so the ring is a loop
    until the next test frame closes it again. With the 200ms profile (20 ms x 3 = 60 ms
    monitoring) that is one to several test periods of loop per closure.
  - `show mrp ring` never shows it: every sample reads Closed or Open as expected;
    Topology Change Count stays 3. Only traffic and the syslog show the loop.
  - Same mechanism as T28863 (member reload/rejoin); this case shows that no stack
    event is needed: a plain link restore does it, and so does the post-boot ring-up.

